  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "game-description-372dfce2-b8d2-4bf3-9df3-34f8437480b0-0",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "Soccer, or association football, is a team game organized around moving a ball into the opponent’s goal. Players primarily use their feet, with passing, dribbling, positioning, and coordinated movement creating attacking opportunities. Standard outdoor play uses eleven players per side, including a goalkeeper with special handling privileges within the penalty area."
    },
    {
      "id": "game-description-372dfce2-b8d2-4bf3-9df3-34f8437480b0-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "The Football Association’s 1863 rules were an important step in distinguishing association football from other football codes. The game itself developed collectively from earlier traditions, and informal versions adapt its recognizable goals and movement to streets, small pitches, and widely varying numbers of players."
    },
